  MU [neutral]: Micron (MU) shares fell about 3.96% on November 13, 2026, in a broader chip-sector selloff that headlines tie to Jensen Huang's resignation as Nvidia CEO. The company's latest guidance called for about $61.5 billion in quarterly revenue, and one headline notes it posted record results. Coverage also describes the stock as down about 20% over the past month but up 16% over the past five trading sessions.
  LITE [neutral]: Marvell Technology has agreed to acquire Lumentum in an all-stock deal valued near $115 billion, with Lumentum holders to receive 4.5 Marvell shares per share and closing not expected until 2028. Lumentum trades well below the value of that offer, with the spread reported at about 18% to 19.7% in recent headlines. Lumentum is up 56% in 2026 but nearly half off its October high.
